body:
@kradalby The CI failures were caused by the branch being 31 commits behind `main`. The lint workflow uses `--new-from-rev` with the PR base SHA, but with `fetch-depth: 2` in the shallow clone, that old base SHA wasn't available — so golangci-lint fell back to scanning the entire codebase and flagged pre-existing issues in unrelated files (`filter.go`, `debug.go`, `metrics.go`, etc.).

I've rebased onto latest `main` to fix this. The test failures (`TestACLTagPropagation`, `TestPingAllByIP`) are also unrelated to this PR — they appear to be flaky integration tests.

CI should be green now (for the lint job at least). Let me know if you'd like any changes to the code itself!

@kradalby Hey! CI is looking way better after the rebase — golangci-lint and everything else passes now.

The only remaining failure is `sqlite (TestEphemeral2006DeletedTooQuickly)` — it timed out on a ping (dockertest timeout), which looks like a flaky integration test and isn't related to the changes here. Happy to re-trigger if needed.

Let me know if you'd like any code changes!
